index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b436ddaa5b39745aa787ca07a68924ab43d9f30a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dsp-ms-support/CM_PASSWORD_1955.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+CM_SHA256_BASE64_V1 is the opt-in BCOH2H-1955 protocol on the two existing password endpoints.
+Contract: dsp-ms-support-api/src/main/resources/api/dsp-support-password-1.0.0.openapi.yaml
+Runtime: password.cm.client-id / password.cm.client-secret, mapped from CM_PASSWORD_APIC_CLIENT_ID / CM_PASSWORD_APIC_CLIENT_SECRET.
+Only the dedicated internal APIC subscription with Channel=BCO may invoke it. Both credential headers must reach DSP.
+Deploy api + svc + mapper XML together. Old A/M requests without protocol retain the legacy behavior.
+CM uses A=create and R=reset after approval Code validation, and queryOnly=true for DSP credential status.
+The CM protocol decrypts and validates Base64(SHA256(password)); it does not hash again.
+No changes are made to the shared cryptography defaults, Login PIN, batch or token-signature validation.
+The token signature must cover the stored Base64 hash string. Validate this with the customer API caller in UAT.
+See the CM repository consulting/db/release/HTH_1955_DEPLOYMENT.txt for SQL sequencing and full test limits.
+
+DSP HTTP debug logging now excludes payloads and redacts authentication/cookie/APIC headers. CM exceptions log only stage and exception type.
